          "path": "_m/u/9/9/z/monastery-of-the-holy-trinity-vilnius-wp/the-church-of-the-holy-trinity.jpg",
          "filename": "The Church of the Holy Trinity (9654554122).jpg",
          "caption": "Information board by the Basilian gate and Church of the Holy Trinity in Vilnius:\n\nThe buildings of the church and Basilian monastery, arranged around a yard, compose a harmonious ensemble, formed over several centuries. The Gothic church, built in 1514, with the elements of the Byzantine style, dominates. From the 17th century the church belonged to the Uniates, or Greek Catholics, for more than 200 years. In the 18th century, after a fire, it was remodelled by the addition of the two Rococo towers. In the 19th century it was given to the Russian Orthodox Church, and at the end of the 20th century it was returned to the Uniates. The most wonderful and ornate part is the gate, the most famous example of Vilnius Rococo architecture, which was built in 1761 by J. K. Glaubitz.",
          "alt": "Information board by the Basilian gate and Church of the Holy Trinity in Vilnius:\n\nThe buildings of the church and Basilian monastery, arranged around a yard, compose a harmonious ensemble, formed over several centuries. The Gothic church, built in 1514, with the elements of the Byzantine style, dominates. From the 17th century the church belonged to the Uniates, or Greek Catholics, for more than 200 years. In the 18th century, after a fire, it was remodelled by the addition of the two Rococo towers. In the 19th century it was given to the Russian Orthodox Church, and at the end of the 20th century it was returned to the Uniates. The most wonderful and ornate part is the gate, the most famous example of Vilnius Rococo architecture, which was built in 1761 by J. K. Glaubitz.",
